To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we will structure the goals and tasks hierarchically. Here's the breakdown:

### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                        | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | --------------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food to Inpatient Room    | Ensure food is delivered from kitchen to inpatient room.            | -                  | Perform   | -        |
| G2      | Determine Retrieval Capability    | Assess if the inpatient or a helper can retrieve food.              | -                  | Query     | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Food                      | Deliver food to the inpatient room table or robot tray.             | FALLBACK(G3.1, G3.2) | Achieve  | G1       |
| G4      | Retrieve Meal                     | Handle meal retrieval by inpatient, companion, nurse, or another robot. | #                  | Perform   | G3.2     |
| G5      | Indicate Meal to Retrieve         | Indicate which meal should be retrieved if necessary.               | -                  | Achieve   | G4       |
| G6      | Track Meal Retrieval              | Track when and where each meal was retrieved.                       | -                  | Achieve   | G4       |
| G7      | Alert on Wrong Meal Retrieval     | Alert if a wrong meal is retrieved.                                 | -                  | Achieve   | G4       |
| G8      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes             | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                | -                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G9      | Coordinate Dish Retrieval         | Coordinate dish retrieval with robots and/or humans.                | #                  | Perform   | G8       |
| G10     | Open Room Door                    | Open the room door for delivery or retrieval tasks.                 | FALLBACK(G10.1, G10.2) | Achieve  | G3.1, G8 |

### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location       | Number of Robots |
| ------- | ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | -------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Inpatient Room | Move to the designated inpatient room for delivery or retrieval.     | AND      | Inpatient Room | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Deliver Food to Table     | Place the food on the room table.                                    | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT3     | Deliver Food to Tray      | Place the food on the robot tray.                                    | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT4     | Retrieve Dish             | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                 | AND      | Inpatient Room | [1, n]           |
| AT5     | Coordinate with Human     | Cooperate with a human to retrieve dishes or open the door.          | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |
| AT6     | Coordinate with Robot     | Cooperate with another robot to open the door or retrieve dishes.    | AND      | Inpatient Room | 2                |
| AT7     | Open Door                 | Open the room door for delivery or retrieval tasks.                  | AND      | Inpatient Room | 1                |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G3, G8 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G4 [IF inpatient/helper cannot retrieve, ELSE G3.1]**
- **G3 -> G3.1 [Sequential], G3.2 [Parallel]**
- **G3.1 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**
- **G3.2 -> G4, G5, G6, G7 [AND]**
- **G4 -> AT3 [IF tray delivery], AT4 [IF dish retrieval] [AND/OR]**
- **G5 -> AT7 [IF door needs opening]**
- **G8 -> G9 [AND]**
- **G9 -> AT4, AT5, AT6 [OR]**
- **G10 -> AT7 [IF door needs opening]**

This goal model captures the hierarchical decomposition of the mission into goals and tasks, considering the necessary cooperation and uncertainty in human and robot interactions.
